 "captions": [
  {
   "id": "B1.c1",
   "beat": "B1",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 5.6,
   "e": 11.6,
   "text": "Every 30 seconds of a night's sleep gets a label: Wake, N1, N2, N3 or REM. Experts score them by hand."
  },
  {
   "id": "B1.c2",
   "beat": "B1",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 12.3,
   "e": 17.1,
   "text": "Can a computer read sleep from one EEG channel, a single pair of scalp electrodes?"
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.c1",
   "beat": "P1",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 18.6,
   "e": 23.4,
   "text": "One pipeline. Input: a single Fpz-Cz EEG channel, 100 samples a second, all night."
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.c2",
   "beat": "P1",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 24.1,
   "e": 29.6,
   "text": "Process: cut into 30-second epochs, make a frequency picture of each, then a CNN and a BiGRU."
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.c3",
   "beat": "P1",
   "c": 3,
   "s": 30.3,
   "e": 33.9,
   "text": "Output: one of five stages for every 30 seconds, a hypnogram."
  },
  {
   "id": "B2.c1",
   "beat": "B2",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 36,
   "e": 41.9,
   "text": "A 2026 paper in Scientific Reports reports about 83% accuracy from one channel, chaining four ideas."
  },
  {
   "id": "B2.c2",
   "beat": "B2",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 42.6,
   "e": 46.7,
   "text": "We set out to reproduce it. Within our time and compute, we could not."
  },
  {
   "id": "B2.c3",
   "beat": "B2",
   "c": 3,
   "s": 47.4,
   "e": 52.7,
   "text": "The paper splits epochs at random, so one person can be on both sides. We split by person."
  },
  {
   "id": "B2.c4",
   "beat": "B2",
   "c": 4,
   "s": 53.4,
   "e": 59.8,
   "text": "Why? A new patient is a new person. A random split can reward recognising the person, not reading the sleep."
  },
  {
   "id": "B3.c1",
   "beat": "B3",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 61.3,
   "e": 68.1,
   "text": "So we changed the question: does it still work on a person the model has never seen, and can we explain every step?"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q2.c1",
   "beat": "Q2",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 69.8,
   "e": 75.9,
   "text": "Scope: not a replication or clinical validation. Twenty people, one public dataset, unseen people only."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q2.c2",
   "beat": "Q2",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 76.6,
   "e": 83.2,
   "text": "Hypothesis, formed after the baseline failed: nights differ in signal strength, so per-night scaling should help."
  },
  {
   "id": "B3b.c1",
   "beat": "B3b",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 84.9,
   "e": 92.9,
   "text": "Our data is Sleep-EDF, public on PhysioNet: healthy adults recorded at home on cassette recorders, usually two nights of about 20 hours."
  },
  {
   "id": "B3b.c2",
   "beat": "B3b",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 93.6,
   "e": 101,
   "text": "Trained technicians scored every 30-second page of each whole night by hand, following the 1968 Rechtschaffen and Kales rules."
  },
  {
   "id": "B3b.c3",
   "beat": "B3b",
   "c": 3,
   "s": 101.7,
   "e": 106.7,
   "text": "Two experts can disagree, so these labels are a trusted reference, not perfect truth."
  },
  {
   "id": "B3b.c4",
   "beat": "B3b",
   "c": 4,
   "s": 107.4,
   "e": 114.3,
   "text": "We use 20 people and 39 nights: 42,307 epochs. Trimmed to its scored span, a night is about 1,085 epochs, or 9 hours."
  },
  {
   "id": "D2.c1",
   "beat": "D2",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 115.3,
   "e": 122.2,
   "text": "Three variables: the EEG signal, the stage label, and a person ID that only splits the data and never feeds the model."
  },
  {
   "id": "D2.c2",
   "beat": "D2",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 122.9,
   "e": 129.8,
   "text": "Limits: healthy adults only, just 20 people, human-scored labels and one channel. This data cannot speak for patients."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1.c1",
   "beat": "M1",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 131,
   "e": 138.3,
   "text": "STFT: a 2-second Hamming window slides in 1-second steps, turning each epoch into a 129 × 29 picture of frequency over time."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1.c2",
   "beat": "M1",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 139,
   "e": 145.6,
   "text": "Why frequencies? Sleep stages are defined by rhythms: slow waves mark N3, spindles N2, alpha waves relaxed wake."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1.c3",
   "beat": "M1",
   "c": 3,
   "s": 146.3,
   "e": 154.1,
   "text": "The paper uses a synchrosqueezed transform. We chose STFT because we can draw, compute and check it by hand. We never compared them."
  },
  {
   "id": "M2.c1",
   "beat": "M2",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 155.1,
   "e": 162.3,
   "text": "CNN: three blocks of 32, 64 and 128 channels squeeze each picture into 128 numbers. Its limit: it sees one epoch at a time."
  },
  {
   "id": "M3.c1",
   "beat": "M3",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 163.5,
   "e": 169.3,
   "text": "BiGRU: two layers read 20 neighbouring epochs forwards and backwards, because sleep is a sequence."
  },
  {
   "id": "M3.c2",
   "beat": "M3",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 170,
   "e": 175.5,
   "text": "Why? Sleep comes in long runs, so an epoch is easier to judge with its neighbours than alone."
  },
  {
   "id": "M3.c3",
   "beat": "M3",
   "c": 3,
   "s": 176.2,
   "e": 180.8,
   "text": "The cost: it uses future epochs, so it works offline only, never in real time."
  },
  {
   "id": "M4.c1",
   "beat": "M4",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 181.8,
   "e": 188.7,
   "text": "Contrastive learning trains the CNN's embedding: epochs that should match are pulled together, the rest pushed apart."
  },
  {
   "id": "M4.c2",
   "beat": "M4",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 189.4,
   "e": 194.9,
   "text": "It adds a second training phase with many settings to tune, so it costs more time and compute."
  },
  {
   "id": "M4.c3",
   "beat": "M4",
   "c": 3,
   "s": 195.6,
   "e": 202.2,
   "text": "We dropped the paper's contrastive stage: reproducing it failed, and we wanted a chain we can check step by step."
  },
  {
   "id": "M4.c4",
   "beat": "M4",
   "c": 4,
   "s": 202.9,
   "e": 206.8,
   "text": "We never ran that comparison, so we do not claim it helps or hurts."
  },
  {
   "id": "M5.c1",
   "beat": "M5",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 207.8,
   "e": 214.8,
   "text": "Testing is by person: ten folds, with 16 people training, 2 choosing the checkpoint and 2 tested. Nobody appears twice."
  },
  {
   "id": "M5.c2",
   "beat": "M5",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 215.5,
   "e": 219.1,
   "text": "Only two test people per fold, so scores swing between folds."
  },
  {
   "id": "E1.c1",
   "beat": "E1",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 220.1,
   "e": 226.7,
   "text": "Baseline first: macro-F1 56.42%, 95% interval 48.26 to 63.44. Accuracy 65.00%. Folds swing from 39.95% to 74.39%."
  },
  {
   "id": "E1.c2",
   "beat": "E1",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 227.4,
   "e": 233.6,
   "text": "Opening single nights, three were right on only 7.22%, 18.60% and 19.01% of epochs. The average hid them."
  },
  {
   "id": "E2.c1",
   "beat": "E2",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 234.6,
   "e": 241.2,
   "text": "The baseline already z-scored each frequency, but with one ruler: the mean and spread of the 16 training people."
  },
  {
   "id": "E2.c2",
   "beat": "E2",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 241.9,
   "e": 247.2,
   "text": "R1 gives every night its own ruler: that night's own mean and spread, with no labels used."
  },
  {
   "id": "E2.c3",
   "beat": "E2",
   "c": 3,
   "s": 247.9,
   "e": 255.3,
   "text": "Same architecture, retrained: macro-F1 74.86%, interval 71.33 to 78.03; accuracy 80.99%. Gain +18.44, interval 10.07 to 27.55."
  },
  {
   "id": "E2.c4",
   "beat": "E2",
   "c": 4,
   "s": 256,
   "e": 259.6,
   "text": "The three failing nights recover to 82.54%, 88.68% and 84.87%."
  },
  {
   "id": "E3.c1",
   "beat": "E3",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 260.6,
   "e": 267.5,
   "text": "But R1 reads each test night's unlabeled signal and was chosen after the baseline failed. It is offline and post-hoc."
  },
  {
   "id": "E3.c2",
   "beat": "E3",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 268.2,
   "e": 276.6,
   "text": "Whole-recording statistics give 71.84%: −3.02 versus R1, interval −7.12 to +1.22. It crosses zero: no clear difference, not proof of equality."
  },
  {
   "id": "E4.c1",
   "beat": "E4",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 277.6,
   "e": 286.3,
   "text": "N1, the lightest sleep, stays weak: R1 recovers 44.69% of true N1 and 38.91% of its N1 calls are right. Three fixes on validation were all rejected."
  },
  {
   "id": "L1.c1",
   "beat": "L1",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 287.5,
   "e": 294.2,
   "text": "What we can say: in these 20 people an average can hide failing nights, and per-night scaling helped in this test."
  },
  {
   "id": "L2.c1",
   "beat": "L2",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 295.3,
   "e": 301.1,
   "text": "What we cannot say: that it works on new people, since R1 is offline and was chosen after the fact."
  },
  {
   "id": "L2.c2",
   "beat": "L2",
   "c": 2,
   "s": 301.8,
   "e": 307.7,
   "text": "Nor that 80.99% beats or matches the paper's 83%, that it is clinically ready, or that N1 is solved."
  },
  {
   "id": "L2.c3",
   "beat": "L2",
   "c": 3,
   "s": 308.4,
   "e": 312,
   "text": "None of the 78 audited participants is certified independent."
  },
  {
   "id": "L3.c1",
   "beat": "L3",
   "c": 1,
   "s": 313,
   "e": 320.1,
